  "formalRouteSelection": "CHS is the broad humanities and social science expression of the generic degree. Its compulsory culture, history and social theory courses make the breadth identifiable before looking at UCR. The six formal majors in the annual guide include GHIS. There is no stable health generator in these 33 target rows.",
  "newFinding": "Checked 2026-11-13. Current BA-LAGC confirms 45 EC first-year core + 85 EC major + 10 EC electives + 30 EC minor/additional electives/semester abroad + 10 EC Global Citizenship. Three first-year choice courses total 15 EC; one counts toward another requirement. They are not another 15 EC on top of the 180 EC framework. Seven original core units remain 45 EC, with Mathematics for Social Networks as one allowed maths choice. Add the independently established 10 + 30 + 10 EC categories without inventing specific electives, a minor or a Global Citizenship selection. The supported inventory is 95 EC; the remaining 85 EC major allocation is under review. CHS remains the neutral broad humanities/social-science major for the generic degree, selected before UCR matching. Current public CHS text and the 2026–2027 image grid confirm cultural expressions, historical processes, social forms, research design and a capstone. The annual major API expressly limits 15/40 EC to class2028 and 10/45 to classes2026/2027. Forward2271 returns current2261 bytes. Current capstone8004CS001Y is JSON null. Actual linked university-host PDF grid is404; old org/student-host guesses also404. The current public structure confirms supervised independent capstone research and cross-cultural Global Citizenship, and limits an internship to5EC; these known facts are not erased by the unresolved exact capstone load. Accessible OER/handbook are2025–2026, with old10EC thesis and final-semester120EC auto-enrolment; do not apply that progression to2029. The previous complete comparator and three UCR options are retained byte-exactly as research, not active unverified comparison/alignment. All56 actual current-UCR contributions and three feasible schedules remain reusable; prior DynamicEarth/EnergySustainability repair retained. No app or Excel changes.",
  "essentialGap": "Confirm the Culture, History and Society major requirements for September 2026 entrants, expected class of 2029: the capstone credit load, corresponding additional-major-course allocation, and thesis entry/progression. The current major catalogue specifies 15 EC capstone + 40 EC additional courses only for class of 2028, and 10 + 45 EC for classes of 2026 and 2027. Its generic 85 EC major and academic core are established, but the applicable cohort allocation is not. The capstone module returns JSON null. The linked 2026–2027 PDF grid returns 404; the public 2026–2027 image grid shows subjects and a 400-level capstone, without credits or cohort rules. The accessible OER and student handbook are explicitly 2025–2026, not an adopted 2029 bridge. Preserve the verified 95 EC outside the major and all substantive research. Do not borrow another major’s onwards wording, silently apply either old capstone version, or infer no-match.",
  "noMatch": false
}
